  "decisionSummary": "The dev-publish v12/0.0.12 source is canonical. v11/0.0.11 PROVED the keybox fix on the tenant \u2014 fresh grain 9YDbi96t8xLoxLaGBaz5gK created keybox.json (417 bytes, which v10 never managed) and logged 'keybox open (... created=true)' with zero keybox errors \u2014 and then died on the very next line of that same first start with 'sqlitestore: pragma \"PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL\": unable to open database file: out of memory (14)'. SQLite 14 is SQLITE_CANTOPEN: WAL needs a shared-memory mapping and the supervisor's default RLIMIT_AS starves it for a Go+capnp process. This cut adds requestedMemoryGiB = 4, the same lever Bureau Doc 2.0.37 and Teleport 1.3.6 needed and which is proven end-to-end for both. It removes the CAUSE rather than weakening Jinn's deliberate creation-authority rule (F-267).",
